    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919-a1">

                <pb facs="1082" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg986"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Ambassador</hi>: With reference to your
                    letter to Mr. Villiers of July 9, respecting the reported presence of a Spanish
                    privateer near Queen Charlotte Sound, Lord Salisbury desires me to say that a
                    telegram has been received from Lord Aberdeen reporting that <pb facs="1083"
                        n="987" xml:id="pg987"/> H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Icarus</hi> has
                    made a thorough search of the territorial waters of Canada on that coast but has
                    seen and heard nothing of the vessel in question.</p>
                <p>Believe me, yours, very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">T. H. Sanderson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
